d area of ombrotrophic blanket bog isolated from groundwater and surface inflow through substrate topography. As well as extensive C. vulgaris cover, typical peat-forming vege- tation is present; Eriophorum spp. and Sphagna including S. capillifolium, S. papillosum and S. cuspidatum.","sitenotes":null,"geography":"{\"type\":\"Point\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[-2.0961,54.34556]}","altitude":480,"collectionunitid":32407,"collectionunit":"OM177","handle":"OM_OM177","unittype":"Modern","datasets":[{"doi":["10.21233/vxq4-xt89"],"agerange":[{"units":"Calendar years BP","ageold":-62,"ageyoung":-62}],"database":"Neotoma Testate Amoebae Database","datasetid":45594,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"A.","contactid":6308,"firstname":"Antony","familyname":"Blundell","contactname":"Blundell, Antony"},{"initials":"A.A.","contactid":14022,"firstname":"Anatoly A","familyname":"Bobrov","contactname":"Bobrov, Anatoly A"},{"initials":"B.G.","contactid":105,"firstname":"Barry G.","familyname":"Warner","contactname":"Warner, Barry G."},{"initials":"D.J.","contactid":7252,"firstname":"Daniel J.","familyname":"Charman","contactname":"Charman, Daniel J."},{"initials":"E.A.D.","contactid":9337,"firstname":"Edward A. D.","familyname":"Mitchell","contactname":"Mitchell, Edward A. D."},{"initials":"G.","contactid":7272,"firstname":"Gunnar","familyname":"Mallon","contactname":"Mallon, Gunnar"},{"initials":"G.T.","contactid":11443,"firstname":"Graeme","familyname":"Swindles","contactname":"Swindles, Graeme"},{"initials":"J.","contactid":15631,"firstname":"Joseph","familyname":"Holden","contactname":"Holden, Joseph"},{"initials":"M.","contactid":7267,"firstname":"Mariusz","familyname":"Lamentowicz","contactname":"Lamentowicz, Mariusz"},{"initials":"M.J.","contactid":7245,"firstname":"Matthew J.","familyname":"Amesbury","contactname":"Amesbury, Matthew J."},{"initials":"R.J.","contactid":6543,"firstname":"Richard","familyname":"Payne","contactname":"Payne, Richard"},{"initials":"T.E.","contactid":604,"firstname":"T. Edward","familyname":"Turner","contactname":"Turner, T. Edward"},{"initials":"T.P.","contactid":13988,"firstname":"Thomas P.","familyname":"Roland","contactname":"Roland, Thomas P."},{"initials":"Y.A.","contactid":9442,"firstname":"Yuri","familyname":"Mazei","contactname":"Mazei, Yuri"}],"datasettype":"testate amoebae surface sample","datasetnotes":null,"recdatecreated":"2019-08-06T16:51:09"}]}},{"site":{"siteid":26164,"sitename":"Thornton Moor","sitedescription":"Minerotrophic basin mire of around 7.1 ha which has an area of ombrotrophy in the centre (Honeyman, 1985). The site has been fenced off to prevent stock from entering the area and is therefore only subject to minimal grazing by lagomorphs, resulting in a relatively undisturbed bog surface. Vegetation is typically Calluna–Eriophorum type, with abundant bryophytes including S. cuspidatum, S. capillifolium, S. papillosum, S. palustre, H. jutlandicum, Pleurozia schreberi and Rhytidiadelphus squarrosus. A number of Salix spp. trees are growing to maturity at the fen–bog transition zone.","sitenotes":null,"geography":"{\"type\":\"Point\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[-2.07139,54.27806]}","altitude":417,"collectionunitid":32408,"collectionunit":"ThM178","handle":"TM_THM178","unittype":"Modern","datasets":[{"doi":["10.21233/vr05-8v12"],"agerange":[{"units":"Calendar years BP","ageold":-62,"ageyoung":-62}],"database":"Neotoma Testate Amoebae Database","datasetid":45595,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"A.","contactid":6308,"firstname":"Antony","familyname":"Blundell","contactname":"Blundell, Antony"},{"initials":"A.A.","contactid":14022,"firstname":"Anatoly A","familyname":"Bobrov","contactname":"Bobrov, Anatoly A"},{"initials":"B.G.","contactid":105,"firstname":"Barry G.","familyname":"Warner","contactname":"Warner, Barry G."},{"initials":"D.J.","contactid":7252,"firstname":"Daniel J.","familyname":